From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Sinyavin <sinyavin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 20:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: qcom: emac: register the dedicated MDIO child

An Ethernet controller node may contain both the standard fixed-link child
and the devices present on its MDIO bus.  Passing the controller node to
of_mdiobus_register() makes the MDIO core mistake fixed-link for a PHY and
probe it at every unoccupied address.

Use a dedicated mdio child when present, while retaining compatibility with
existing device trees that put PHY children directly below the controller.

Signed-off-by: Dmitry Sinyavin <sinyavin@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/emac/emac-phy.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/emac/emac-phy.c
@@ -133,9 +133,14 @@ int emac_phy_config(struct platform_devi
 		if (adpt->phydev)
 			get_device(&adpt->phydev->mdio.dev);
 	} else {
+		struct device_node *mdio_np;
 		struct device_node *phy_np;
 
-		ret = of_mdiobus_register(mii_bus, np);
+		mdio_np = of_get_child_by_name(np, "mdio");
+		if (!mdio_np)
+			mdio_np = of_node_get(np);
+		ret = of_mdiobus_register(mii_bus, mdio_np);
+		of_node_put(mdio_np);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_err(&pdev->dev, "could not register mdio bus\n");
 			return ret;
